  "body": "**Description**\r\n\r\nAdds a first-class llama.cpp (llama-server) integration and a matching widget, so dashboards can monitor any OpenAI-compatible llama.cpp server over its plain HTTP endpoints \u2014 no extra sidecar required.\r\n\r\n**What it does**\r\n\r\n- New integration (`packages/integrations/src/llama-cpp/`): connects to llama-server's built-in endpoints\r\n  - `/health` \u2014 liveness\r\n  - `/v1/loads` \u2014 model name, context size, KV cache\r\n  - `/metrics` \u2014 Prometheus gauges: token generation rate, prompt processing rate, load\r\n  - `/slots` \u2014 per-slot KV cache usage and in-flight request state\r\n- New widget (`packages/widgets/src/llama-cpp/`): model name + status, generation speed with a three-tier display (in-request running average \u2192 live gauge \u2192 process-lifetime average, with tooltip explaining which is shown), context/KV cache usage with optional per-slot breakdown\r\n- API route, request handler, definitions registration and translations (en/zh/cn) wired in\r\n- 21 unit tests for the integration's response mapping, including per-request speed calculation\r\n\r\n**Why per-request running average?**\r\n\r\nllama-server's `/metrics` rate gauge resets to 0 while idle and reflects a rolling bucket while busy, so a dashboard polling it cannot tell \"fast now\" from \"fast earlier\". The widget instead diffs `next_token[0].n_decoded` across polls for the slot's current `id_task` (verified against llama.cpp source, `server-context.cpp`), giving the true average speed since the current request started \u2014 matching what the llama.cpp Web UI shows during generation.\r\n\r\n**Manual testing performed**\r\n\r\n- [x] Integration tested against a real llama-server (b10679-1) running a Qwen 27B GGUF (n_ctx 131072): health, loads, metrics and slots endpoints verified\r\n- [x] Per-request speed verified end-to-end: `id_task` stable during a generation, `n_decoded` increases 0\u2192137 over ~4.4s (~31 t/s), resets on request end\r\n- [x] Widget deployed on a production Homarr instance (Docker, NAS) \u2014 KV usage, speed tiers and tooltips render correctly across busy/idle transitions\r\n- [x] `pnpm turbo run build` (3/3), typecheck (4 packages), lint and format all green; 21/21 integration unit tests pass\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nNone \u2014 this is self-contained: it only adds new files plus the standard registration points (definitions, translations, exports).\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added a llama.cpp integration for monitoring local LLM server health, loaded models, request activity, generation speed, context usage, and token metrics.\n  * Added a configurable llama.cpp dashboard widget with model details, status, performance, and cache statistics.\n  * Added an AI integration category with English, Simplified Chinese, and Traditional Chinese translations.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added setup and configuration guides for the llama.cpp integration and widget.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
